     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 4, \"rationale\": \"The target can be reached through four branches: shareMount, codeRepo, vaultRead and dbReplica. The shareMount branch (kerberoast -> backupHost -> shareMount) shares no useful node with the other branches, so it needs its own block. With that block placed, the other three branches need at least two more. Blocking codeRepo first still leaves serviceAccount (and domainAdmin) reaching vaultRead or dbReplica. Blocking jumpHost or sshKey first still leaves printServer (via configSecret) and monitoringHost (via rdpLogin), which share no common blockable node. No set of 3 works. A valid set of 4 is kerberoast, jumpHost, configSecret and rdpLogin.\"}"
    }
